==Description==

Increase profits with time spent as this class, time skipped and with experience gained, increase evocation efficiency with time skipped and time spent as this class. Has access to powerful spells and upgrades directly affecting profits. Possesses upgrades that decrease basic costs of sources. Has access to Compressed Time resource, used for spells with time distortion effects.

Unique [[Sources|Source]]: Ley Temporal Singleton, a combination of {{ClassTooltip|Prodigy|display_name=Prodigy's}} Ley Apex and {{ClassTooltip|Chronomancer|display_name=Chronomancer's}} Temporal Anchor, both of which replaces The Nexus.

Upon reaching [[Paragon]] 42, Temporalist may take on either [[Ascension Forms]]: {{ClassTooltip|Demiurge}} or {{ClassTooltip|Dread}}.

==Basic Design==
Temporalist combines the insane timeskips of [[Chronomancer]] with the high numbers and profits of [[Prodigy]]. As a result, Temporalist is the king of buildup, with such combinations as the source cost reduction upgrades of prodigy and the ability to use {{SpellTooltip|spell_name = Refined Wormhole}} to rapidly max those sources with [[Simulacrum]], or using [[Pixie]] to rapidly build up autoclicks. Combine these with charging {{SpellTooltip|spell_name = Synthetic Entity}} faster than it can be cast (which can also be boosted by {{SpellTooltip|spell_name = Primal Power}}!), and Temporalist can collect every form of character XP at an insane rate.

Temporalist also trades in {{SpellTooltip|spell_name = Wormhole}} for {{SpellTooltip|spell_name = Refined Wormhole}}, which doesn't clear active spells.{{SpellTooltip|spell_name = Refined Wormhole}} charges based on your current time distortion, encouraging you to use {{SpellTooltip|spell_name = Temporal Distortion|display_name = Temporal Distortion}} to maximize your time distortion. These can be combined to stack [[Prodigy|Prodigy's]] incantations much faster, such as {{SpellTooltip|spell_name = True Sorcery}} and {{SpellTooltip|spell_name = Quasi-incantation}}.

While bursting, Temporalist can leverage his high level, number of sources, and time skipped to boost incantations such as {{SpellTooltip|spell_name = Alter The Laws}}, {{SpellTooltip|spell_name = Primal Power}}, {{SpellTooltip|spell_name = Converge Timelines}}, {{SpellTooltip|spell_name = Ley Overdrive}}, and {{SpellTooltip|spell_name = Superposition}}, which all benefit from stacks of {{SpellTooltip|spell_name = Quasi-incantation}}. He can also boost his level with {{SpellTooltip|spell_name = True Sorcery}}, which scales off casts this exile. This is an excess of powerful incantations, leaving Temporalist with more options than he can even cast on once! And that's without even including weaker incantations such as {{SpellTooltip|spell_name = Ritual Of Power}}, or evocations such as {{SpellTooltip|spell_name = Kelphior's Black Beam}}, {{SpellTooltip|spell_name = Singularity Beam}}, or {{SpellTooltip|spell_name = Refined Wormhole}}.

Overall, Temporalist is a powerful class, with incredible versatility and more options than he can even leverage at once. He's undeniably the strongest class for collecting [[Achievements]], and for pushing to higher character levels, while also being potent for earning profits if you can balance his many talents.

